dialogue-snapshots
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-17
what: stop a Dialogue step being O(journal). Two parts, because the
  warm path and the cold path are different problems.
  WARM: `step(p, a)` advances a Paused the caller is ALREADY holding -
  journal the answer, then one `Delim.answer` - so a drive is O(n)
  total instead of O(n squared). `run(oracle)` uses it.
  COLD: snapshots. A continuation cannot be snapshotted, so what is
  written is the journal PREFIX (Chapter(upTo, answers)) into a
  compacted keyed topic, the Snapshots convention; `recovered` then
  reads one record plus the tail instead of all N.
  What stays O(n) and why: the program is re-run once on a cold start.
  That is exactly what "the fold is the program" costs, and it is
  stated rather than hidden.
  MEASURED: a counting Topic in the test asserts run(oracle) reads far
  fewer records than a loop of replay-based answer, and that a
  snapshotted cold start reads a bounded number.
files: okay-persist/src/main/scala/okay/persist/Dialogue.scala,
  okay-persist/src/test/scala/okay/persist/TestDialogue.scala,
  specs/persist.md, CHANGELOG.md
